"""
Daedalus Vault by Jason Bocaling: a password-locked encrypted file vault for Windows.

    pip install PySide6 cryptography
    python daedalus_vault.py
    (installer for other PCs: run build_installer.bat, see README.txt)

Security model
  * Password -> Scrypt (n=2^15, r=8, p=1, random 16-byte salt) -> 256-bit key.
  * Every file is encrypted with AES-256-GCM in 4 MiB chunks (per-chunk nonce,
    final-chunk flag authenticated, so truncation/reordering is detected).
  * The file index (names, sizes, MIME types) is encrypted too.
  * Files are only reachable by clicking the vault and entering the password.
  * The key lives in memory only while unlocked; Lock/close discards it.
  * Open: images are decrypted in memory only; other files go to a private temp
    folder and open in their normal app. Edits are saved back into the vault and
    the temp copy is wiped when you Lock (close the app first).
"""
